// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
// Filename:	TS058 290-024 CL Auto 2 Power PCB.test
// Project:		CL Auto 2
// Author:      Foster & Freeman Ltd - Paul Evans
// Modified:    04/11/25
//
// Description: This script test the Power swithing and checks the ouptu signals for the SMARC to read.
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

{0} force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.
#1: Equipment Setup 1.
a. Connect the Bus Priate and PSU to the test PC.
b. Connect the Bus Priate to TE261 Part A test jig.
c. Connect the UUT to the TE261 Part B.
d. Connect the UUT & Part B to the test battery.
e. Enter the PCB serial number.
CLICK_OK:


#2: Equipment Setup 2 & Configure the PSU.
a. Connect the TE016 power lead to the DC jack on the PCB.
b. Connect the Red (TE016 positive)lead to the + of channel 1 on the PSU.
c. Connect the Black (TE016 negitive)lead to the - of channel 1 on the PSU.
d. Set the TENMA Programmable PSU power switch to on.
CLICK_OK:
CONNECT: TENMAPSU
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #1: 
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCP1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCPSET1:1.750
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:15.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:1.500
CLICK_OK:

#3: Connect and Configure the Bus Pirate.
CONNECT: BUS_PIRATE
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #3:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE m4
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE 3
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE W // sets the power rail to on, and drives a voltage to pin 5 C_PWR_ON

#4: Power on button.
a. On the side of TE261 Part B, press the power on button.
b. Check the battery voltage is showing on the voltage display ?
CLICK_OK:

#5: Check if DC is PRESENT.
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE @
READLINE: BUS_PIRATE AUX
Expected result is = I2C>@AUX INPUT/HI-Z, READ: 1
************************
The returned current is =  %AUX%
************************
PASS_FAIL:

#6: Check charging circuit.
a. Check the charging LED is showing.
b. Check the voltage display is showing the PSU (DC) voltage 14.9-15V.
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1
PASS_FAIL:

#7: Check not DC(PSU) is not PRESENT.
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE @
READLINE: BUS_PIRATE AUX
Expected result is = I2C>@AUX INPUT/HI-Z, READ: 0
************************
The returned current is =  %AUX%
************************
PASS_FAIL:

#8: Check the charging circuit is active.
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE d
READLINE: BUS_PIRATE ADC
Check that the returned Voltage is below 1V.
************************
The returned current is =  %ADC%
************************
PASS_FAIL:

#9: Check the power switching. 
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
Check the battery voltage is now showing on the voltage display.
PASS_FAIL:


#10: Check the Not Charging signal is high.
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE d
READLINE: BUS_PIRATE ADC
Check that the value is between: 2.30-2.40V
************************
The returned current is =  %ADC%
************************
PASS_FAIL:

#11: Turn off. 
a. Press and hold for ten seconds
b. Check the voltage display turns off. 
PASS_FAIL:

#12: Test complete
IF: %FAILED% > 0
GOTO: #Failed:
ELSE: #Passed:

#Failed: A test failed.
a. This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
b. Check the Log file for more details on the failed test(s).
IMPORTANT: This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
//DISPLAY: test_failed.png
CLICK_OK:
GOTO: #QUIT:

#Passed: Test's Complete.
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish and power OFF.
//DISPLAY: AllTestsPassed.png
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET2:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET2:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE w
DISCONNECT: TENMAPSU
DISCONNECT: BUS_PIRATE
// End of file
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -